# systemd USER preset policy for this device.
#
# Same trap as taimen.preset, one scope over: postmarketos-base-systemd's
# trigger runs presets for user units too, and pmOS's default policy is
# "disable *". A user unit this package ships without an enable line here is
# silently switched off on the next install or upgrade. Observed on the
# r20->r24 upgrade, which printed
#   * Removed '/etc/systemd/user/default.target.wants/pipewire-pulse.service'.
# and took the PulseAudio socket -- and therefore callaudiod -- with it.
enable pipewire-pulse.service
